{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-5194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2x+2y+{y}^{2}+1=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-5194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+2y+{y}^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}+2y) & =-1 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =-1+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={1}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-1)$ and its radius is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-5194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "518919be3ed98ee1caaa53ef16f521216a6452e46d5c78e54a1b65227153e542"} {"question" "q-5194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-5194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-1,-1)$, radius: $1$"] ["text" "center: $(-1,-1)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(0,1)$, radius: $1$"] ["text" "center: $(1,0)$, radius: $2$"] ["text" "center: $(1,1)$, radius: $1$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-5194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(-1,-1)$, radius: $1$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n$2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4x+4y & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}+4y) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4) & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{(y+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{(y-(-2))}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-2)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "518919be3ed98ee1caaa53ef16f521216a6452e46d5c78e54a1b65227153e542"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(-2,2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(2,2)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(2,4)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5x-3y-8=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5x-3y-8 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x)+({y}^{2}-3y) & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & =8+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{33}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{33}{2} \\\\ {(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "518919be3ed98ee1caaa53ef16f521216a6452e46d5c78e54a1b65227153e542"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{5}{2},-\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{33}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$"] ["text" "center: $(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{33}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-14620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}=55+10y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2} & =55+10y \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =55 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =55+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,5)$ and its radius is $9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "518919be3ed98ee1caaa53ef16f521216a6452e46d5c78e54a1b65227153e542"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-1,-5)$, radius: $9$"] ["text" "center: $(-1,5)$, radius: $9$"] ["text" "center: $(-5,1)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(1,5)$, radius: $3$"] ["text" "center: $(5,-1)$, radius: $7$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(-1,5)$, radius: $9$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-24x+{y}^{2}+6y=-137.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-24x+{y}^{2}+6y & =-137 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-24x)+({y}^{2}+6y) & =-137 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 12x+{12}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}) & =-137+{12}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 12x+{12}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-12)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-12)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(12,-3)$ and its radius is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "518919be3ed98ee1caaa53ef16f521216a6452e46d5c78e54a1b65227153e542"} {"question" "q-15468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041465/state.json" "file_sha256" "74a2978edc6b2e750782c26a6485eb597a5bd3f5e8b53bdef2ca740ebfb18b62"} {"question" "q-15468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-12,-3)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(-3,12)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(12,-3)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(12,3)$, r